{
  "status": "SAMPLES. Synthetic values only. The responses are the output of the governance policy engine for the test configuration, not of a running service, not a policy release, not runtime validation.",
  "purpose": "Reusable pre-tool check request and response pairs for consumers: Nour's contract test (success and failure paths), Malak's result fixtures and Mohab's route test.",
  "source": "Derived from the combined cases of policy-matrices.json (spec section 5.1) and kept in step with them by a test. Governance contract section 4.1 and 4.2 name the fields.",
  "notes": [
    "The request carries only the fields the three policies read. The full Trace Schema v1.9 policy_check event has more (the authorization snapshot, evidence references, ids and the attempt). This is not that event.",
    "Amounts are decimal strings. The threshold used by these samples is the test value 1000.00 USD, not the policy value.",
    "response.evaluated_policies[].reason_code is the governance reason code of every result. Trace Schema v1.9 has failure_or_error_reason for FAIL and ERROR only: the platform adapter maps those codes to it and keeps the codes of PASS and NOT_APPLICABLE results in observed_evidence (agreed with Mohab on 2026-11-24).",
    "policy_version is the per-rule version from the configuration and policy_bundle_version is the policy set's id and version. The values here are those of the test configuration, not of the policy configuration.",
    "observed_evidence lists the values each policy looked at, as text. It is not the full source evidence.",
    "The responses are the real engine's output for each request, kept in step by a test."
  ],
